<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Sabah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1752–</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as House of Sabah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a> is the ruling family of Kuwait, descended from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-utbah">Bani Utbah</a> clan that settled there in the early 18th century. Sabah I became the first sheikh around 1752. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubarak-al-sabah">Mubarak the Great</a> the family placed Kuwait under British protection in 1899, and it has ruled the independent State of Kuwait since 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-sabah.jpg" alt="Al Sabah" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AK Alrabah · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_State_of_Kuwait.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
